# Environment

Filled by `aw-harness-init` / `install.sh`. Edit `docs/_harness/tools/env.local.sh` if the machine changes.

## Topology

| Item | Value |
|---|---|
| Stack | `{{STACK_KIND}}` |
| Runtime | `{{AW_RUNTIME}}` (`docker` = PHP in container; `host` = PHP on the machine) |
| Magento root on the host | `{{MAGENTO_ROOT}}` |
| Magento version | **{{MAGENTO_VERSION}}** |
| Compose / stack directory | `{{COMPOSE_DIR}}` (project name `{{COMPOSE_PROJECT}}`) |
| PHP container / process | `{{PHP_CONTAINER}}` |
| Magento path in runtime | `{{RUNTIME_MAGENTO_ROOT}}` |
| Aheadworks code path | `{{MAGENTO_CODE_PATH}}` |
| Start hint | `{{STACK_HINT}}` |

### Docker stacks (markshust / pystacker / other)

If `{{PHP_CONTAINER}}` is not running, ask the user to start the stack (`{{STACK_HINT}}`). Do not start Docker yourself unless the user asks.

Typical Mark Shust:

```bash
cd {{COMPOSE_DIR}}
bin/start
bin/cli bash
bin/magento cache:flush
```

Typical compose / pystacker:

```bash
cd {{COMPOSE_DIR}}
docker compose up -d
docker exec -it {{PHP_CONTAINER}} bash
```

### Host PHP

Gates run with `cd {{MAGENTO_ROOT}}` and the host `php` / `vendor/bin/*`. Ensure `vendor/` is installed on the host.

## Harness tools

From Magento root (`{{MAGENTO_ROOT}}`):

```bash
docs/_harness/tools/drift.sh <Module>
docs/_harness/tools/gates.sh <Module>
docs/_harness/tools/sync.sh --module <Module>   # docker volume layouts only
docs/_harness/tools/check-harness.sh
docs/_harness/tools/cbm-index-module.sh <Module>
```

Overrides live in `docs/_harness/tools/env.local.sh` (sourced by `env.sh`).

## MCP

- **magento-wiring** — project `.cursor/mcp.json` (`MAGENTO_ROOT` / `MAGENTO_CODE_PATH`).
- **codebase-memory-mcp** — user-level Cursor MCP (snippet: `.cursor/mcp.user-codebase-memory.snippet.json`).
- Wiring UI (optional): from the wiring MCP home, `MAGENTO_ROOT=… .venv/bin/magento-wiring-ui` → http://127.0.0.1:9750/

## Project-specific notes

Fill after install (examples from SoT / your project):

- Modules **without** `.git` (no MR): list them here.
- Blocked / dangerous modules (e.g. `Aheadworks_Sarp3Server` if enabling it breaks REST/GraphQL/cron): document the stop condition here.
- Bind-mount vs volume layout details for `app/code`, `vendor/`, etc.

## Test infrastructure

- Run PHPUnit with `docs/_harness/tools/phpunit/phpunit.xml` (gates copy it into the runtime).
- Do not configure integration tests without user approval.
- Do not assume payment sandbox credentials or storefront theme without checking the project.
